217 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 191 0 R
/E (1\) Fashion has a Data Aggregation Problem. Fashion is a creative field involving work across photos, sketches, tech-packs, BOMs, Fit notes, Colorways etc. across informal channels like emails, WhatsApp, teams. Existing Systems require people to upload changes manually and coordinate different PLMs and ERPs.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
218 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 191 0 R
/E (2\) Software is not built for fashion. Fashion has a complex operational plane on steroids spread across different roles and workflows which are deeply connected and actively making changes. All teams work on different tools today, and use PLM systems primarily for data management. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
219 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 191 0 R
/E (3\) There is no way to track product change. A change \(costing, fit, colorways, BOM, delivery dates, quantity, launch timing\) creates a chain reaction across the business. This chain reaction is tracked all manually through PDFs, spreadsheets, handwritten notes, phone calls etc.  leading to follow-ups, invisible changes and planning gaps and causing late launches, missed sales and cannibalization. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
